eos-3.8" change_id="I3dbeaacad46cdf2097d7df25d1353aa1b824d6b4" commit="9a4f66a23bc6d19a9bc6bec3c71b489c6fe7a50c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: gpu: mali: Fix enum type mismatch in kbase_mem_from_umm()  In kbase_mem_from_umm() the value BASE_MEM_IMPORT_TYPE_UMM of type 'enum base_mem_import_type' is assigned to a variable of the enum type 'kbase_memory_type'. Use the value to KBASE_MEM_TYPE_IMPORTED_UMM of the correct type instead.  BUG=none TEST=build for peach  Change-Id: I3dbeaacad46cdf2097d7df25d1353aa1b824d6b4 Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/481051 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="481051" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/481051/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I33eb4eff035d31d462f339d61cd119b9335211f2" commit="f3982524138b1527a1c1bfc9d69602ea3e4ed34b" commit_message="network_WlanDriver: drop fixed interface name list; ask shill instead  We really shouldn't be keeping a fixed list of potential device names. It's more flexible and easier to just ask shill anyway, so let's do that.  This incidentally fixes some quirks of the 'interface' API, which caused us to dump a spurious log message when checking for the description:  04/12 14:41:50.819 ERROR|         interface:0171| Device description not supported on non-wifi interface: wlan0.  This also stops pretending that the test actually handles multiple interfaces properly.  BUG=none TEST=`test_that ... network_WlanDriver` with Wifi enabled, and with Wifi      module forcibly unloaded (to see 'TestNA')  Change-Id: I33eb4eff035d31d462f339d61cd119b9335211f2 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/481439 Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="481439" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/481439/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I01d9f7172e53ea089bc00f426f2c4976a2cba16c" commit="624a57daa93deee8fe7dcc65eb8bfdd3a44da528" commit_message="rsync: upgraded package to upstream  Upgraded net-misc/rsync to version 3.1.2 on amd64, arm, x86  BUG=chromium:710111 TEST=for b in link bob x86-generic; do   FEATURES=test emerge-$b -q --nodeps net-misc/rsync; done The tests don't pass on arm (didn't pass for 3.1.1 either), so I also deployed onto a bob device and did some basic checking.  Change-Id: I01d9f7172e53ea089bc00f426f2c4976a2cba16c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/480996 Commit-Ready: Benjamin Gordon &lt;bmgordon@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benjamin Gordon &lt;bmgordon@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chirantan Ekbote &lt;chirantan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="480996" owner_email="bmgordon@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" ref="refs/changes/96/480996/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4e54ec69bc980cd31df42f4f78743f7563d95c5c" commit="7788c553c7e21bc3d6aabfe521dacdb5e0b149a0" commit_message="cr50: send '\n' before issuing commands  When using the cr50 console through the servo header cr50 may be asleep when you are trying to issue a command. Send '\n' to wake up cr50 before sending the real command  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=turn off the ap, wait 20 seconds, and run dut-control ccd_lock. login wait a while and then run dut-control ccd_lock.  Change-Id: I4e54ec69